00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:01.510 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  cameroon's indomitable lions score again  bringing victory to the national  football team in the african cup of  nations opening game against burkina  faso  it's really reassuring we're happy this  proves that we live up to our name the  lions we are really happy and emotional  with this victory  while burkina faso put up a fight some  of their best players were not on the  pitch but in their hotel rooms in  isolation after testing positive for  covid health workers woke them up for  tests on saturday night hours before the  game  much to the dismay of burkina faso's  team  according to the afcon health protocols  if i'm not mistaken the tests must be  carried out 48 hours before a match  we did the tests yesterday at 11 pm so  if my calculations are correct we will  not be within the 48 hours for  tomorrow's match  players from several african nations  including the favorite senegal have  tested positive hours after the opening  ceremony it seems omicron is already  overshadowing the event  the government spent almost a billion  dollars to host the african cup of  nations while fans are being tested  before entering the stadiums containing  the virus in a country where most are  unvaccinated and the health system is  underfunded will be a challenge  security is also a concern  english-speaking separatists were  responsible for bomb blasts last week in  limbe where several games are expected  to take place  there are also threats of attacks from  boko haram in the country's north  additional forces including the military  have been deployed to both regions  i can't reveal here the measures that  are being put in place but you should  know that afghan will also take place  under very good conditions there are no  varies there is nothing to worry about  despite the spread of covid and the  threat of attacks of armed groups  organizers say the show must go on  cameroon sees in the event an  opportunity to unite cameroonians and  for a brief 90 minutes forget about the  worries at home and enjoy the game  nicholas hawk al jazeera

